learning a programming language when you already have one or two or
more under your belt is a substantially different proposition to
learning one when you have none. I could probably pick up functional
Dutch in a similar persiod of time, but only because I happen to have
gone through formal training in other languages, and so know how
grammar works and the things that I will need to learn and apply. Most
native English speakers don't have much grammar training, and so would
need the concepts of grammar taught before they can even approach the
specifics of any particular language.

